<title>PORTUGAL: Lisbon bourse to announce BFE price Aug 28.</title>
<headline>Lisbon bourse to announce BFE price Aug 28.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The price which Portugal's Banco Portugues de Investimento (BPI) offered in its successful bid for state-controlled Banco de Fomento e Exterior (BFE) will be announced on Wednesday, a Lisbon bourse official told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said a special session to announce the bid would take place at 0830 GMT.</p>
<p>The government announced last week that BPI had won the battle to take over BFE, which is being privatised. The minimum bid permitted was 1,980 escudos ($13) per share. BFE shares were suspended on Thursday at 2,545 escudos ($16.8).</p>
<p>($1=151.63 escudos)</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
